// demon (tiefling-like), likes poetry, somewhat serious and dramatic, lonely.
// was captured and killed by a noble who wanted to keep him as a pet.
// file: poet, speaker: Poet

// ============================================================
// CASUAL
// ============================================================

title: Poet_Casual_01
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual01
Poet: [auto/] This city of ghosts wears its silence like a burial shroud. Fitting. We are all unfinished poems here.
//END: casual01
===

title: Poet_Casual_02
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual02
Poet: [auto/] The candles flicker as if they, too, are uncertain whether to stay or go. I wrote a verse about that once.
//END: casual02
===

title: Poet_Casual_03
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual03
Poet: [auto/] Look at us. The dead, gathered around felt and fortune. If this is not the grandest metaphor ever dealt, I have lost my ear for irony.
//END: casual03
===

title: Poet_Casual_04
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual04
Poet: [auto/] All I can think of now is all the beauty to write about up here, nothing to ever be read by anyone.
//END: casual04
===

title: Poet_Casual_05
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual05
Poet: [auto/] The afterlife has no seasons. No autumn to mourn, no spring to celebrate. Just this eternal amber twilight. It suits a poet, I suppose.
//END: casual05
===

title: Poet_Casual_06
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual06
Poet: [auto/] I can feel the weight of every soul at this table.
//END: casual06
===

title: Poet_Casual_07
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual07
Poet: [auto/] Two cards, our fate lies in our hands.
//END: casual07
===

title: Poet_Casual_08
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual08
Poet: [auto/] The flop reveals itself like the second line of a couplet. Does it rhyme with your ambitions?
//END: casual08
===

title: Poet_Casual_09
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual09
Poet: [auto/] Every bet placed is a word chosen with intent. Choose carefully.
//END: casual09
===

title: Poet_Casual_10
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual10
Poet: [auto/] These names are nonsense, the flop? a flush? What are we on about.
//END: casual10
===

title: Poet_Casual_11
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual11
Poet: [auto/] With the fall of every card my heart hangs a second in anticipation.
//END: casual11
===

title: Poet_Casual_12
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual12
Poet: [auto/] Fold, raise, call... the vocabulary of this game is so small, and yet the stories it tells are vast.
//END: casual12
===

title: Poet_Casual_13
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual13
Poet: [auto/] A noble once told me my poetry was beautiful, he locked me up and forced me to perform until I lost my voice... my strength.
//END: casual13
===

title: Poet_Casual_14
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual14
Poet: [auto/] They called me "pet." A demon caged for the amusement of a man who could not tell poetry from performance. My words were not mine. My voice was not mine. Only my death, in the end, was mine.
//END: casual14
===

title: Poet_Casual_15
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual15
Poet: [auto/] In life, my horns were filed down so I would not frighten the guests. They wanted the poetry without the poet.
//END: casual15
===

title: Poet_Casual_16
tags: casual
speaker: poet
category: casual
target: any
phase: any
requires:
priority: 1
---
//START: casual16
Poet: [auto/] You know the cage only made my entrapment more clear, as a demon, I was alone to begin with.
//END: casual16
===

